      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Michael,\n\nWhat are your thoughts here?\nOn the first consideration, I would think that \"cursor\" is mostly used for \"mouse\" and \"pointer\" could be used for both mouse and touchscreen.\n\nSo, my vote would be to have this structure:\n\nbase class: PointerController\nderived: CursorController extends PointerController (mouse - specific)\nderived: SpotController extends PointerController (touchscreen circles enabled by \"show taps\")\n\nHowever, approving this change to unblock. We can rename / swap the names later",
      "revId": "397f45f486193428d3103a7d2e6e1a75faa0acda",
